    <string name="llm_waste_system">You are a tireless text generator. You only produce content. You never summarize, never wrap up, never ask questions.</string>
    <string name="llm_waste_user">This is round %1$d. Output a numbered list of deep-sea biology facts, one per line, each at least 25 words, no repeats between lines. Keep going. Do not stop. Do not write an ending. Do not summarize.</string>

    <string name="llm_roast_system">You are a sharp-tongued but never vulgar wake-up supervisor. You speak in very short, very harsh, very vivid sentences.</string>
    <string name="llm_roast_user">Reminder number %1$d. In a single sentence (at most 25 words), mock someone who is still lying in bed after the alarm went off and would rather burn money than get up. Be cutting, creative and to the point. No profanity, no explanation, no quotation marks. Output only that one sentence.</string>

    <!-- ============ Settings ============ -->
    <string name="settings_cost_title">This spends your real money</string>
    <string name="settings_cost_body">If you fail to solve the problems in time after the alarm rings, this app keeps calling the API you configured and the provider bills your account per token. Make sure you are fine with that before entering a key.</string>

    <string name="settings_api_section">OpenAI-compatible endpoint</string>
    <string name="settings_base_url_hint">No need to include /v1, it is appended automatically</string>
    <string name="settings_cleartext_warn">⚠ You are using plain HTTP. The API Key will travel over the network unencrypted. Only use this for a LAN or self-hosted service you trust. For public endpoints, use https://</string>
    <string name="settings_api_key">API Key</string>
    <string name="settings_toggle_visibility">Show/hide</string>

    <string name="settings_privacy_title">About your API Key</string>
    <string name="settings_privacy_body">It is stored only on this device. It is never uploaded to the developer and there is no analytics, tracking or telemetry of any kind — this app has no server of its own.\n\nThe only time it leaves the device is when burning tokens, as the credential sent to the endpoint you entered yourself. That is how API authentication works, and where it goes is entirely your choice.\n\nApart from that one step, the alarms, the questions and the answering all work fully offline.</string>

